From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 16:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rgw: drop upload_id from multipart parent span name

The multipart parent span was created with name() as its span name.
For the multipart finalize path, name() returns
"multipart_upload <upload_id>" — so every upload produces a unique
span name. Downstream, Tempo's metrics-generator emits one
Prometheus series per (service, span_name), so the
traces_spanmetrics_* series count grows unbounded with the number
of multipart uploads.

The upload_id is already preserved as a span attribute on the
request span (UPLOAD_ID, set on the line just above). Duplicate
that attribute onto the multipart parent span and use a constant
operation name so multipart_upload aggregates into a single series.
This preserves TraceQL filtering by upload_id while bounding
prometheus cardinality to op-type granularity.

Signed-off-by: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
---
 src/rgw/rgw_op.cc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/rgw/rgw_op.cc b/src/rgw/rgw_op.cc
--- a/src/rgw/rgw_op.cc
+++ b/src/rgw/rgw_op.cc
@@ -4459,7 +4459,10 @@ void RGWPutObj::execute(optional_yield y)

     s->trace->SetAttribute(tracing::rgw::UPLOAD_ID, multipart_upload_id);
-    multipart_trace = tracing::rgw::tracer.add_span(name(), upload->get_trace());
+    multipart_trace = tracing::rgw::tracer.add_span("multipart_upload", upload->get_trace());
+    if (multipart_trace) {
+      multipart_trace->SetAttribute(tracing::rgw::UPLOAD_ID, multipart_upload_id);
+    }
     // propagate multipart trace context so RADOS data writes link to
     // the multipart upload trace rather than the ephemeral request trace
     if (multipart_trace && multipart_trace->IsRecording()) {
--
2.52.0
